# Privacy Policy for splatty-v2

**Effective Date:** June 9, 2026

Welcome to **splatty-v2** (the "Bot"), an automated assistant built on the Reddit Devvit platform designed to compile and archive daily posts under a centralized megathread, keeping subreddits organized and clean.

We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting it. This Privacy Policy describes how the Bot operates, the limited information it processes, and our commitment to data safety.

---

## 1. Information We Process

The Bot is designed as a utility tool for subreddit moderators. It operates strictly within the boundaries of the Reddit platform and processes only the following technical information:

### A. Subreddit Configuration Data
To operate, the Bot requires configuration settings entered by subreddit moderators via the Devvit Settings panel. This includes:
*   **Flair Text to Watch:** The specific post flair used to queue posts for roundup.
*   **Thread Settings:** Customized title templates, body text, and posting schedules (hours and minutes).
*   **Moderation Options:** Toggles deciding whether to lock, remove, or pin roundup posts.
*   **Disable Scheduler Toggle:** A setting to suspend or resume scheduled daily jobs.

### B. Reddit Subreddit Thread Metadata
The Bot uses Reddit's API to track posts matching the target flair, submit the compiled posts as comments under a new daily megathread, and clean up/lock the original posts. It processes and caches post IDs (`t3_...`) to track and organize the daily archive.

---

## 2. What We Do NOT Collect

*   **No Personal Identifying Information (PII):** The Bot does not collect, record, or store personal user information such as real names, email addresses, geographical locations, or IP addresses.
*   **No Reddit Account Credentials:** The Bot operates under Reddit's secure OAuth framework via Devvit. It does not have access to, nor does it collect, passwords or private account credentials.
*   **No User Communication Logs:** The Bot does not harvest or monitor user comments, private messages, or chat histories beyond the titles/bodies of submissions specifically flaired for archiving.

---

## 3. Data Storage & Security

All subreddit settings and active game-tracking metadata are stored natively within **Reddit's secure Devvit infrastructure** (using Reddit's Settings and Redis KV storage APIs).

*   Data is stored on Reddit's servers and is subject to Reddit's overall security controls.
*   No external databases or servers are hosted or managed by the Bot developers to store subreddit or user data.
*   Subreddit moderators have full control and can wipe all Redis tracking data immediately using the **Debug: Clear Storage** tool in their Subreddit Tools panel.

---

## 4. Third-Party Services

Because the Bot is hosted on Reddit and interacts with external APIs, the following third-party privacy policies also apply:
*   **Reddit:** Subject to the [Reddit Privacy Policy](https://www.reddit.com/policies/privacy-policy).
*   **Discord:** The Bot transmits operational status logs (such as success alerts, error messages, and scheduled job queue statistics) to a centralized Discord server via webhook to monitor the health and performance of the Bot. No personal identifying information (PII) of subreddit users is ever transmitted. All transmissions are subject to the [Discord Privacy Policy](https://discord.com/privacy).

---

## 5. Changes to This Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our Bot operations or platform updates. Any updates will be posted directly to the Bot's official source repository or documentation pages.

---

## 6. Contact Us

If you have any questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy or the Bot's operations, please contact the subreddit moderators or open an issue on the Bot's official repository.
